  "map_info": {
    "name": "Vectors_Act1_WhatAVectorIs",
    "lookup_name": "Vectors_Act1_WhatAVectorIs",
    "title": "Vectors in your hands",
    "description": "Carry the known grabbable PointBody through three stations in one room. First move one point relative to its local origin: read displacement, length and a separate unit direction. Next move two points and follow a then b to the rose sum; compare the route length with the direct arrival. Finally project onto the signed X rail and retain the perpendicular remainder. Live labels follow the inputs. Thin cylinders give direction a visible body. These are geometric operations; a moving point does not yet imply a force simulation.",
